      "id": "theverge-2026-09-29-this-might-be-our-first-look-at-google-s-pixel-11a",
      "title": "This might be our first look at Google’s Pixel 11A",
      "summary": "The only noticable difference is that the camera oval is shorter. | Image: Android Headlines\t\n\nGoogle isn't making any significant design changes to its upcoming midrange Pixel update, judging by the leaks shared by Android Headlines. The image renders made by OnLeaks are potentially our first look at the Pixel 11A, which aside from having a slightly rounder oval-shaped rear camera module, looks a",
      "body": "Google isn’t making any significant design changes to its upcoming midrange Pixel update, judging by the leaks shared by Android Headlines. The image renders made by OnLeaks are potentially our first look at the Pixel 11A, which aside from having a slightly rounder oval-shaped rear camera module, looks almost indistinguishable from both the Pixel 10A and Pixel 9A.\nIt seems the chunky display bezels sported by those predecessors will also carry over as they’re present in these leaked images. It makes the phone look very dated compared to the wider Pixel 11 series lineup, but a previous report from Mystic Leaks suggests the Pixel 11A will at least get a much needed spec upgrade to Google’s Tensor G6 instead of retaining the old Tensor G4 processor that appeared in both the Pixel 9A and 10A.\nAndroid Headlines reports the Pixel 11A will be available in four colors: black, silver, green, and purple. We won’t know the exact shades or full specification and price details until it’s officially unveiled by Google, which is expected in Spring 2026 in line with the previous midrange launches.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Google",
        "Google Pixel",
        "News",
        "Tech"
      ],
