      "id": "techcrunch-2026-09-25-meta-opens-early-access-program-for-new-muse-features",
      "title": "Meta opens early access program for new Muse features",
      "summary": "Anyone interested in joining has to ask Muse to put them on the list.",
      "body": "1:34 PM PDT · September 25, 2026\nImage Credits:Samuel Boivin/NurPhoto (opens in a new window) / Getty Images\nAfter announcing a host of new features for Meta’s Muse AI app at its Connect 2026 developer conference this week, the company is opening up requests for early access. Meta shared on Friday that you can now ask Muse to put you on the list to try out its latest capabilities before anyone else.\nMeta posted a link to a prompt on X that, when shared with Muse, will log that you’re interested in joining Meta’s early access program.\n(If you don’t want to click through, you can just copy and paste the prompt: “Can you let the Muse team know I want to be part of the Muse early access program?”)\nWhile typically companies offer pilot tests or betas with select users, they often A/B test with a randomized group to gain feedback and measure results. In this case, however, Meta is looking for AI enthusiasts to try its features first. That tactic could help it stay ahead of the competition, given that this crowd tends to use multiple AI apps and agents and has a good understanding of the market.\nAs to what the new features will be? Meta teased many of those at Connect, including the launch of a digital avatar for Muse that you’ll be able to video chat with, tons more shopping partnerships and connectors, and an expansion of the Muse Mac app, which will soon be able to use your computer to complete various tasks.\nThe company also said that Muse would be coming to Meta’s lineup of AI glasses, so users can interact with the agent just by speaking a wake word, then issuing a command.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Sarah Perez",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-25T20:34:53.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/meta-muse-finger-on-app-GettyImages-2293791808.jpg?w=1024",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/25/meta-opens-early-access-program-for-new-muse-features/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
