      "id": "theverge-2026-09-23-xbox-s-mythic-achievements-sound-like-playstation-s-platinum",
      "title": "Xbox’s Mythic Achievements sound like PlayStation’s Platinum trophy",
      "summary": "Xbox appears to be ready to launch its own version of PlayStation's platinum trophies. A new update to the Xbox PC app has revealed Mythic Achievements, which according to data in the app will appear once a player completes all the Achievements in a game.\nMythic Achievements appear on screen with a unique unlock sound, and players will reportedly be able to track them through the Xbox dashboard. X",
      "body": "Xbox appears to be ready to launch its own version of PlayStation’s platinum trophies. A new update to the Xbox PC app has revealed Mythic Achievements, which according to data in the app will appear once a player completes all the Achievements in a game.\nMythic Achievements appear on screen with a unique unlock sound, and players will reportedly be able to track them through the Xbox dashboard. Xbox players will also be able to display their Mythic count on their profiles. Some Xbox Insider testers have already started spotting references to Mythic Achievements in early versions of the Xbox dashboard.\nXbox CEO Asha Sharma revealed last month that Xbox would be getting a platinum trophy equivalent later this year. Microsoft still hasn’t officially announced Mythic Achievements, but if they’re already starting to appear in early Xbox software then you can bet they’ll turn up officially very soon.\nMythic Achievements started appearing in the Xbox PC app on the same day Microsoft announced it was laying off 268 Xbox staffers, likely closing Ninja Theory, and moving Halo, Sea of Thieves, and Age of Empires over to Activision.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Gaming",
        "Microsoft",
        "News",
        "Tech",
        "Xbox"
      ],
      "author": "Tom Warren",
