    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-09-23-stunning-photos-from-across-the-uk-capture-the-first-day-of-",
      "title": "Stunning photos from across the UK capture the first day of astronomical autumn",
      "summary": "In the northern hemisphere, the September equinox occurred in the early hours of Wednesday marking the start of astronomical autumn.",
      "body": "The word \"equinox\" comes from Latin and means equal night. At the equinox, the daylight measurement is taken from the point when the centre of the Sun is at the horizon, and is 12 hours sunrise to sunset and 12 hours sunset to sunrise.However, it is the top edge of the Sun which is visible first at sunrise and last at sunset.Because of light refraction - light being bent by the atmosphere - there is still light for a time when the Sun is not directly visible. This adds extra time to daylight hours.In autumn, this means that the time when day and night are actually equal happens after the equinox.This is known as the \"equilux\", which means equal light. This year, that happens in the UK on Friday 25 or Saturday 26 September, depending on your latitude.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-23T11:11:19.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_weather/1200/cpsprodpb/9aad/live/7a02ce70-b735-11f1-b1d1-571ed4d7ff2c.jpg",
