      "summary": "China is competing with the United States and other nations to develop AI.",
      "body": "Homepage    Accessibility links   Skip to content   Accessibility Help     BBC Account      Notifications        Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live               More menu             Search Sounds              Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food        Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live         Close menu   BBC SoundsSounds home pageHomeMusicPodcastsMy SoundsUse BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsWorld Service,·22 Sep 2026,·26 minsGauging China's AI strengthTech LifeAvailable for over a yearHow far has China come in developing AI technology? And what challenges does it face? An expert helps us understand the thinking in Beijing.\nAlso this week: what can fifty thousand autonomous machines tell us about the future of robotics? And cutting edge tech helps cricket reach new audiences.",
